Z||000000||rnoswal||10-05-2000||10:05 PM||||Felt a little sporty with the 85 2.5 car today. Even though it needs bushings all around, I took a few slow corners faster than usual. Right and left the car dies halfway through the corner. It does start back up after I start going straight again. The car has 1/4 tank of fuel, according to the guage. I still have the TBI but it feels like a carbed car that is letting the float bowl empty out. Battery is solid in the car and the lights stayed on, it was night time.<BR>Anyone?<P>Russ<P>------------------<BR>Russ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||10-05-2000||10:20 PM||||check th efuseable link on the starter that happend to me once. the wire was loose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||10-05-2000||10:20 PM||||The same thing is happening to my 1984 Fiero right now. I have one other symptom that I wonder if you are having - when my car has warmed up and I turn it off for 15 or 20 minutes, I have to hold the gas pedal to the floor to start it (I've read that this puts the computer into "Flood Mode"). When this began happening, I also began noticing that after I did get it started, it would seem to cut out in turns. I don't notice the cutting out in turns if I haven't started it in "flood mode" since it was off. <P>Maybe our problems are similar and are related to the injector in the throttle body.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rnoswal||10-05-2000||10:29 PM||||Sorry William but my car does seem to start fine hot or cold any time, so far that is. I will check the fuseable link though, because the engine does quit suddenly and starts back up just as fast. It is really raining here now so I guess I will have to check it tomorrow.<P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||SibERThuG||10-05-2000||11:54 PM||||I had that kind of problem with my 88' formula. Come to find out, it was just a fuse under the dash. It died in slower corners and stops. Thats all it was. Luckily.<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-06-2000||10:14 AM||||It could be the pickup going dry because the corner threw the fuel to the side. could be the fuel tank shifting and either messing with the pump wires or pinching the fuel lines.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||10-06-2000||11:10 AM||||Dieing in a corner is dangerous(obviously).  I wrapped a 68 Galaxy around a light pole becuase it died while trying to hang a corner hard.  Damn Ford carberators. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  If it were a mid-engine car, it probably wouldn't have spun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||10-06-2000||12:11 PM||||Russ,<P>I have a few Fiero's and ALWAYS corner hard on and off of the hwy ramps.  About a month ago, my 87 DIS Duke began doing the exact same thing.  When I am testing the lateral G's... right after all 4 of my tires start singing... the check engine light comes on just long enough for me to let off the gas... then she kicks back in.  It happens regardless of how much gas is in the tank in my coupe.  <P>I have been meaning to post about this, but kept forgetting.  This does not make any sense to me... any suggestions?<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||William Federle||10-06-2000||01:18 PM||||Back when I was having electrical problems with my battery wire to the starter shorting out intermittantly, it would make the check engine lite come on (and the shift light) and the tach would jump around. Maybe you have something intermittantly shorting to ground WTIII<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaveL||10-06-2000||03:18 PM||||I almost hate to say it. Quit going around corners fast! That also stops a lot of the noise I usually hear from the direction of the passenger seat too!||||reg||1
